ople. 2. Use content generation to \"finish your thought\" and extend your notes to make them more rich and searchable. 3. Search the web (Wikipedia, Google knowledge graph) for topics & people mentioned in your notes. Append that content to the bottom of your notes to make notes richer, and easily searchable. This is a positive feedback loop that helps make more connections between notes, as well.","topics":[],"score":249780,"global_rank":60162},{"name":"safranchik/shower-thought-lm","owner":"safranchik","html_url":"https://github.com/safranchik/shower-thought-lm","stars":1,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Jupyter Notebook","description":"Language Model to Generate Shower Thoughts","topics":[],"score":249777,"global_rank":60167},{"name":"fiezt/Peer-Review-Bidding","owner":"fiezt","html_url":"https://github.com/fiezt/Peer-Review-Bidding","stars":1,"forks":1,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"Jupyter Notebook","description":"Tanner Fiez, Nihar Shah, Lillian Ratliff. \"A SUPER* Algorithm to Optimize Paper Bidding in Peer Review\" ICML Workshop on Real-world sequential decision making: reinforcement learning and beyond.","topics":[],"score":249774,"global_rank":60175},{"name":"kalpak92/CAP_6610_Machine_Learning","owner":"kalpak92","html_url":"https://github.com/kalpak92/CAP_6610_Machine_Learning","stars":1,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Jupyter Notebook","description":null,"topics":[],"score":249764,"global_rank":60187},{"name":"dbinoy/amazon-sagemaker-keras-text-classification","owner":"dbinoy","html_url":"https://github.com/dbinoy/amazon-sagemaker-keras-text-classification","stars":1,"forks":1,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"Jupyter Notebook","description":" A step-by-step guide that shows how to do text classification by run training/inference for a custom model in Amazon SageMaker","topics":[],"score":249760,"global_rank":60191},{"name":"mileserickson/mongodb_demo","owner":"mileserickson","html_url":"https://github.com/mileserickson